# VS Code REST Client / Thunder Client. Dev container: localhost:3060 on the Docker
# server (or the port VS Code forwards to your workstation), or
# http://account-service-api:8080 from another container on the ew-dev network.
@base = http://localhost:3060
# = ACCOUNT_SERVICE_API_KEY in .env
@key = change-me
# BMS Users.UserId (user_index.user_id) of a test user
@userId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Validate coupon
POST {{base}}/registration/validate-coupon
X-Api-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "couponCode": "EW00000000X" }

### Validate email
POST {{base}}/registration/validate-email
X-Api-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "someone@example.com" }

### Validate username
POST {{base}}/registration/validate-username
X-Api-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "testuser01" }

### Register (use ROBUST_SKIP=true in .env to skip the grid account)
POST {{base}}/registration
X-Api-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "couponCode": "EW00000000X",
  "username": "testuser01",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "someone@example.com",
  "password": "Change1234!",
  "avatarCode": "Glen"
}

### Change password (own change: acting user = the user; or an admin/teacher with isInitial)
PUT {{base}}/users/{{userId}}/password
X-Api-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "actingUserId": "{{userId}}", "actingUserPassword": "Change1234!", "newPassword": "Change5678!" }

### Forgot-password reset (needs a fresh token: CALL dev_ew_system.sp_mint_service_action_token('system:set-password', '<userId>', '<userId>'), valid 30 s)
POST {{base}}/users/{{userId}}/password/reset
X-Api-Key: {{key}}
X-Service-Token: paste-the-token-id
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newPassword": "Change9012!" }

### Login (add "mfaToken": "123456" after MFA_REQUIRED / MFA_INITIAL)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
X-Api-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "testuser01", "password": "Change1234!" }

### MFA QR code (PNG; only while the secret was never verified)
POST {{base}}/auth/mfa/qr
X-Api-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "testuser01", "password": "Change1234!" }
